---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://chartglade.com/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'About', item: 'https://chartglade.com/about/' },
    ],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About ChartGlade"
  description="ChartGlade makes free printable teaching charts — math, sight words and cursive — that print cleanly from the browser with no sign-up."
  path="/about"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>About ChartGlade</h1>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <p>
      ChartGlade started the way most teaching resources do: a parent staring at a multiplication table at 9 p.m.,
      finding fourteen versions online, and discovering that every single one wanted an email address, a download,
      or both — and then printed with a watermark diagonally across the 7s.
    </p>
    <p>
      So we built the version we wanted: charts that render as plain web pages and print as plain letter paper.
      The page is the printable. There is no account, no PDF, no "premium tier," and the print button strips the
      page down to the chart itself before your printer sees it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every chart comes with notes on how it is actually used in classrooms — which facts get memorized first,
      what a good alphabet key word looks like, why cursive is taught in stroke families. We would rather explain
      the teaching than just hand you a grid, because a chart without a routine is decoration.
    </p>
    <p>
      Something missing or printing wrong? <a href="/contact/">Tell us</a> — chart requests are how the library grows.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
